#import "template.typ": *

#let metadata = (
  title: "Solo Navigation",
  unit: "Cross Country Endorsement | Lesson 8",
  author: "C.Moroney",
  version: "v1.0.0",
)

#let lesson = (
title: [#metadata.title]

,aim: [
To plan and conduct a solo navigation exercise that satisfies the v8 Cross Country Endorsement competency variables — including at least one leg of 75 NM from the departure aerodrome, landings at two different locations, and a minimum total duration of two hours — submitting and cancelling SARWATCH.
]


,overview: [
This is the integrating lesson of the Cross Country Endorsement. It addresses elements *1.2 Notification and SARWATCH*, *1.7 Conduct arrival procedures* (including cancel SARWATCH), and brings together *1.1*, *1.3* and *1.8* under solo conditions. The RAAus Navigation/Meteorology exam must be passed before this flight can be carried out. The student plans the entire flight manually, gathers weather/NOTAM and fuel requirements, and briefs the instructor on every aspect before departure. The instructor must confirm the headings and times are sound, that there are no airspace violations, and that the aircraft will not be over inhospitable terrain for extended periods. The student submits a domestic flight plan via NAIPS, sets a reminder to cancel SARTIME, and carries the instructor's mobile number with instructions to land/divert and call if any problem arises.
]

,learning_outcomes: [
#text(size:12pt)[*Knowledge*]
- State the carriage-of-documents, recency and fuel requirements applicable to the flight (RAAus FOM; AC 91-15).
- Explain SARWATCH: submission, the SAR time, amendment, and cancellation responsibilities.
#text(size:12pt)[*Skills*]
- Prepare a complete nav log manually: TR, HDG, ETI, altitudes, fuel and frequencies.
- Submit a domestic flight plan/flight notification through NAIPS and brief SAR information.
- Conduct the solo navigation exercise: intercept track within 5 NM, maintain route, manage fuel, complete waypoint checks, conduct arrivals and two landings at different locations.
- Cancel SARWATCH on completion.
#text(size:12pt)[*Non-Technical Skills*]
- [TEM] Make an independent, conservative go/no-go decision and in-flight ADM.
- [HF] Manage solo workload and self-monitor for overload/fatigue.
- [SA] Maintain SA, lookout and airspace awareness without an instructor present.
- [CRM] Divert, land and call the instructor if required.
]

,theory_knowledge: [
- Documents to be carried *(Pg 245)*; pilot in command *(Pg 253)*; equipment required — serviceable instruments and radio *(Pg 253)*
- Fuel calculations *(Pg 146–148)* — refer FOM
- Classification of airspace *(Pg 260)*; avoiding controlled airspace *(Pg 275)*
- SARTIME *(Pg 274)*
]

,ground_brief_topics: [
Total time: 45 mins \
Equipment required: Student's completed plan and nav log, VNC, ERSA, EFB, PLB, NAIPS access, current GAF/GPWT, TAFs and NOTAM, instructor's or school contact number \

*Non-Technical Skills* (5 minutes)
- [TEM] Conservative solo go/no-go; in-flight decision triggers.
- [HF] Self-monitoring for overload and fatigue when solo.
- [CRM] Divert, land and call the instructor if required; using area frequency for help.

*Plan review* (20 minutes)
- Instructor reviews headings, times, airspace clearances, terrain exposure, fuel (incl. reserve) and daylight; student briefs weather, NOTAM, ERSA and fuel.

*Route confirmation* (10 minutes)
- Confirm the route includes a leg of 75 NM from departure, two landings at different locations, and a minimum 2-hour total.

*SARWATCH* (10 minutes)
- Submit the domestic flight plan via NAIPS; set a SARTIME cancellation reminder; confirm the instructor's or school number.
]

,ground_tasks:[
#text(size:12pt)[*Instructor*]
- Independently verify the student's plan: headings, times, airspace, terrain, fuel and daylight.
- Confirm recency, document carriage and aircraft serviceability.
- Confirm the route satisfies the competency variables before despatch.
- Remain contactable and at the flight school for the duration of the flight.
#text(size:12pt)[*Student*]
- Complete IMSAFE; make and brief an independent go/no-go decision.
- Prepare a complete manual nav log (TR, HDG, ETI, altitudes, fuel, frequencies).
- Submit the flight plan to NAIPS and brief SAR information; set the SARTIME reminder.
]

,in_flight_tasks:[
#text(size:12pt)[*Demonstration*]
- None
#text(size:12pt)[*Student Practice (solo)*]
- Fly the planned route with no diversions unless required for safety.
- Intercept the departure track within 5 NM; record departure time; maintain route and timing.
- Conduct arrivals and two landings at different locations; make correct radio calls per AC 91-10.
- Manage the fuel log and frequencies; complete waypoint checks (CLEAROFF).
- Return with a completed nav log and cancel SARWATCH.
]

,common_errors:[
- *Optimistic go/no-go*: Solo decisions should be more conservative than dual — if in doubt, don't.
- *Forgetting to cancel SARTIME*: Set a reminder and cancel promptly on arrival.
- *Pressing on when unsure*: The rule is land/divert and call — there is no prize for continuing.
]

,post_flight:[
- *Student Self-Assessment*: How the planning held up; any decisions made en route.
- *Instructor Feedback* (10 min):
  - Evaluate against the standards below (S / C / NC).
  - Review the completed nav log and SARWATCH management.
  - Discuss any in-flight decisions and ADM.
- *Scenario Reflection*: "Which part of today's solo would you plan differently next time, and why?"
- *Next Steps*: Where competent across all elements, recommend for the Cross Country Endorsement flight test; otherwise assign targeted further practice.
]

,standards_for_progression:[

#text(size:12pt)[*SOLO REQUIREMENTS*]

_Regulatory requirements (RAAus FOM):_
- ☐ Valid RAAus Pilot Certificate held
- ☐ Valid BFR held
- ☐ Financial flying membership of RAAus current
- ☐ Health declaration current (driver licence medical standard)
- ☐ RAAus Navigation and Meteorology Exam passed (minimum 80%)
- ☐ >12 hours DUAL cross-country training received

_Competency requirements:_
- ☐ All navigation syllabus elements at S standard and recorded in the student records.

_Weather on the day:_
- ☐ Crosswind at all airfields in flight plan \<12 knots
- ☐ Ceiling >2500 ft AGL
- ☐ Visibility >10 km
- ☐ No significant turbulence, windshear, showers, or thunderstorms forecast for the entire route; conditions stable for the duration of planned solo

#text(size:12pt)[*Certificate Standard (C) — mandatory target before flight test*]
- Creates an appropriate, complete manual flight plan and nav log.
- Submits a flight notification/domestic flight plan via NAIPS and manages SARWATCH (including cancellation).
- Safely conducts the solo navex, returning with a complete nav log.
- Route satisfies the v8 competency variables: one leg of 75 NM from departure; two landings at different locations; minimum 2-hour duration; demonstrated use of both DR and GPS/EFB (operational and limited modes) across the course.
- Record S / C.
]

,safety:[
- *Weather*: Conditions clearly within the student's solo limits meets above criteria; conservative margins for forecast deterioration.
- *Altitude*: Suitable VFR cruise levels clear of CTA steps and SUA; minimum 1,500 ft AGL en route; no low-level segment on the solo.
- *Emergency Procedures*: Pre-briefed expectation for diversion/landing and call instructor/school; suitable landing areas and alternates identified; fuel and daylight reserves protected.
- *TEM*:
  - Solo student must self-monitor for overload/fatigue and prioritise aviate-navigate-communicate.
  - Maintain generous buffers from CTA/SUA.
  - Maintain lookout and traffic awareness at both arrival aerodromes.
- *Route*: NOT SUGGESTED ROUTE, MANDATORY: YHEC-YBOA-YTWB-YHEC (TGL at YBOA and YTWB)
- *Aircraft Limits*: Operate within POH/AFM at all times.
]

,homework:[
- Plan the route for the flight test, given by the instructor.
- Read Bob Tait's RAAus Cross Country Endorsement:
  - Documents to be carried (Pg 245); pilot in command and equipment required (Pg 253); fuel calculations (Pg 146–148).
  - Revise classification of airspace (Pg 260) and avoiding controlled airspace (Pg 275).
- Consolidate for the Navigation & Meteorology theory examination (v8 Theory Unit 2.03) and the Cross Country Endorsement flight test.
]
)

